<code>assert c != null => \forall Object e; c.contains(e); this.contains(e);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert c != null => \forall Object e; c.contains(e); this.contains(e);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert c != null => \forall E e; c.contains(e); this.contains(e);</code>

However, since the correct syntax for expressing that every element in the collection `c` is contained in the priority queue after initialization should use the `this.contains(e)` method properly, the corrected assert statement should be:

<code>assert c != null => \forall E e; c.contains(e) => this.contains(e);</code>
--------------------
